  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Nagiyev gathers the kitchen staff to announce the mass firings. Senya and Fedya discuss the depressing situation. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Ребята, нам придётся расстаться с вами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Куда вы собрались так рано?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нас уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Как уволили? Тебя тоже?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, мы все уходим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "А что сказал шеф?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф ничего не сделал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы часто шагаем в пропасть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Это из-за самоуверенности?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, мы слишком много хотели.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Вот ваш расчёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Только двадцать тысяч?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Остальное будет в конце месяца.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Ребята, нам придётся расстаться с вами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Guys, we will have to part ways with you.' You'll hear 'the boys' all the time in the show, here connected with 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Куда вы собрались так рано?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where are you off to so early?' The question word for 'where to' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'early'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нас уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We got fired.' Here 'us' sets up the idea, while 'to fire' comes at the end for emphasis. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Как уволили? Тебя тоже?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'How fired? You too?' In Russian, 'how' leads into 'too' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, мы все уходим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, we are all leaving.' Fedya puts 'we' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'are leaving'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "А что сказал шеф?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what did the chef say?' Senya starts with 'what' and pairs it with 'said' to make the point clear. Then Fedya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф ничего не сделал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The chef did nothing.' Fedya puts 'chef' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'nothing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы часто шагаем в пропасть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We often walk into the abyss.' You'll hear 'we' all the time in the show, here connected with 'to disappear'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Это из-за самоуверенности?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is this because of overconfidence?' There is no question word here — in Russian, rising intonation on 'overconfidence' is enough to make it a question. And Fedya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, мы слишком много хотели.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, we wanted too much.' A compact expression built around 'we' and 'wanted'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Вот ваш расчёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here is your payout.' The first content word means 'final pay', and 'final pay' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Только двадцать тысяч?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Only twenty thousand?' A compact expression built around 'only' and 'thousand'. Dmitry answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Остальное будет в конце месяца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The rest will be at the end of the month.' In Russian, 'remaining' leads into 'months' in a very natural everyday phrasing. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
